; The one zone this bench is authoritative for.
;
; Each name below exists to produce ONE fact certdoctor has to report correctly.
; A name absent from this file gets NXDOMAIN from an AUTHORITATIVE server, which
; is not the same fact as NXDOMAIN invented by a resolver in the middle.
$ORIGIN ok.test.
$TTL 60

@   IN SOA ns.ok.test. admin.ok.test. (
        1          ; serial
        7200       ; refresh
        3600       ; retry
        1209600    ; expire
        3600 )     ; minimum

@   IN NS  ns.ok.test.
ns  IN A   172.28.0.53

; A records and no AAAA. Asking for AAAA gets NOERROR with no answer - NODATA -
; which is a different fact from "the name does not exist" and is one of the
; three certdoctor asks the resolvers directly in order to tell apart.
only4   IN A     192.0.2.10

; Both record types, so the union of the direct view holds four addresses while
; the platform hands back a filtered list.
dual    IN A     192.0.2.20
dual    IN AAAA  2001:db8::20

; The address DNS knows for this name. The verification run also gives the
; container a hosts entry pointing somewhere else entirely, and the two views
; then share no address at all.
split   IN A     192.0.2.30
